  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#46333\", \"PowerToys#48566\", \"PowerToys#34950\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before. PowerToys has no way to exclude specific apps from screen sharing yet. The main tracking issue is PowerToys#46333 (Privacy Overlay). It proposes a utility, similar to Always on Top, that marks chosen windows as excluded from capture, so they stay visible to you but not to Teams or Zoom sharing, recordings or screenshots. PowerToys#48566 was closed as a duplicate of #46333. PowerToys#34950 is an earlier request for the same idea, based on WDA_EXCLUDEFROMCAPTURE. Please subscribe to or upvote #46333 instead of opening a new request. A contributor has built a proof of concept there, but nothing has shipped. Until then, share a single window instead of the whole screen. You could also use the Region to Share app, which is mentioned in #43020.\"}",
